This README file contains a brief description of the verification case.

A simple test for a 1mm x 1mm x 1mm case with:

Temperature: 1200K
density: 2.2 g/cm³
fast neutron flux: 1.25e18 n/m²/s
fluxConversionFactor:0.91  //To have the Ks = 1.996e-29 - 4.415e-32T + 3.6544e-35T²
stress:0.1 MPa

The calculated K = 6.55860484E-30
So the creep_rate = K*stress*flux*fluxConversionFactor = 7.4604130106955E-13 /s
creep_strain at 80e6 s = 5.9683304085564E-05

The average creep_strain obtained by OFFBEAT is -5.96833792E-05, the relative error is 0.00012585502289251%.




The verification of creep in form of creep_rate = K * (sigma1 - vc*(sigma2+sigma3)) * phi 
as well as the solution for principal stress can refer to the case_4b of the Iaea_Benchamark
